/-!
# `prefix_sklansky`: a Sklansky parallel-prefix adder, proved for every `N` with the `sv_comb` tactics

`prefix_sklansky.sv` is a Sklansky (divide-and-conquer) adder written for this example from the textbook
construction (Sklansky, 1960): columns `0 … N` (column `0` the carry in, column `k + 1` bit `k`), `R = $clog2(N + 1)`
rounds of a 2-D generate/propagate pair `G, P : [R:0][N:0]`, round `r` joining every column `k` whose bit `r` is set
(`((k >> r) & 1) == 1`, a conditional generate inside the round and column loops) with the last column of the block
below it, `((k >> r) << r) - 1`, and copying the others; `s[k] = P[0][k+1] ^ G[R][k]`, `cout = G[R][N]`.
`add_proof.lean` proves the svGolf `add` statement for it (`prefix_ks/statement.lean`) at every `N` in the task's
range.

The envelope was generated by `python3.12 extractors/sv/extract.py --top prefix_sklansky
Examples/system-verilog/prefix_sklansky/prefix_sklansky.sv -o prefix_sklansky.sv.json`.

Non-vacuity rows: every input combination at `N = 1, 2, 3, 4`, under the source-order and the reversed schedule, one
`run2` cycle each, against `Nat` arithmetic.
-/

